# TrackNariño Architecture Rules

This project is a production-grade logistics and trucking platform for Colombia.

The system must prioritize:

- Real-time logistics reliability
- GPS tracking stability
- Offline-first behavior
- Security alerts
- Scalability
- Production-ready architecture
- Clean modular code
- Error tolerance
- Premium UX/UI

Mandatory rules:

- Never create duplicated logic
- Never leave TODO placeholders
- Never simulate functionality
- Every screen must connect to real backend data
- Every API endpoint must be validated
- Every async process must handle errors
- All navigation flows must be tested
- Use repository/service architecture
- Separate UI, state, services and models correctly
- Backend must follow controller/service/repository structure
- No hardcoded URLs
- No mock data in production code
- Every feature must support loading, success and error states
- All critical actions must persist correctly in database
